CLAUDE.md
OWNER.md
# CLAUDE.md is a GENERAT of the seven fragments in rulebook/ — they carry the same deploy
# host and IP the monolith did, so they are ignored for exactly the same reason it is.
rulebook/
# graphify (code knowledge graph) — machine-local artifacts, never tracked (public repo + lanes must stay clean)
graphify-out/
# .claude/settings.json is TRACKED since the lane-permission hook (2026-09-13): an ignored file never
# reaches a lane (createWorktree copies only settings.local.json), and the hook exists for lanes. The
# graphify entries rode along with their account-name path replaced by $HOME and a missing-binary exit 0.
# the agent harness drops COPIES of installed skills here (graphify, kriterium-grill, mess-notiz,
# unslop — the originals live in ~/.claude/skills/). Machine-local, and tracking them in a PUBLIC
# repo would publish them; untracked they block every land, which is how this was noticed.
.agents/
inspektion-register.jsonl

# uploads the owner drops into a session (POST /api/slots/:id/upload). Ignored on purpose: an
# untracked file blocks a lane land, and the route REFUSES to write where this line is missing.
# Keeping a drop is then a deliberate `git add -f` — losing it is the default.
drops/

# backups of the deploy identity. `.env` above is ignored, its copies were not: a `.env.bak-<ts>`
# sat untracked in this PUBLIC repo carrying the real host, IP and share URLs (measured 2026-08-22).
# One `git add -A` would have published them.
.env.bak*

# codex hook config: carries a machine-local absolute path (account name), exactly like
# .claude/settings.json above. The hook stays local-only. Exception: `.codex/agents/` holds
# repo-local agent roles (no paths), which codex loads from a trusted project's layer.
.codex/*
!.codex/agents/

# publish transfer artifacts and ad-hoc root screenshots. A bundle's tip is by construction
# already in the history that produced it. And a root PNG is single-session UI evidence:
# released-section.png painted the account path INTO the image, where no grep finds it.
*.bundle
/*.png
